<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady on limited purchases.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady on limited purchases.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets on Monday. Purchasing from processing plants was limited at upper price levels against poor arrivals.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 3,000 tonnes in the markets of central India, which were around 20,000 tonnes per day at the same time last year. Volumes were dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were firm on limited selling from processing plants and refineries. Prices were up by 200-300 rupees per tonne. Volume was limited and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices stayed at previous levels. Soymeal yellow was $271 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $131-132 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,500 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,450-4,475 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
